# 4. Objective Classification

## Purpose

Objective Classification establishes the engineering framework used to organize all System Objectives within the Adaptive Vehicle Intelligence Architecture (AVIA).

The purpose of classification is to improve organization, consistency, scalability, traceability, and long-term management of the objective library.

---

## Classification Principles

System Objectives shall be grouped according to their primary engineering purpose.

Each objective shall belong to one primary objective category while maintaining traceable relationships with other categories where necessary.

Objective categories are organizational structures and shall not restrict engineering interaction between objectives.

---

## Approved Objective Categories

The following objective categories are established for the AVIA project:

| Identifier | Category |
|------------|----------|
| SO-F | Functional Objectives |
| SO-C | Coordination Objectives |
| SO-P | Performance Objectives |
| SO-S | Safety Objectives |
| SO-R | Reliability Objectives |
| SO-H | Human Interaction Objectives |
| SO-A | Adaptability Objectives |
| SO-M | Maintainability Objectives |
| SO-SC | Scalability Objectives |

---

## Category Responsibilities

Each objective category shall:

- Define objectives within its engineering domain.
- Maintain internal consistency.
- Support traceability to the System Objective Specification (SOS).
- Support derivation of System Requirements.
- Comply with this governance document.

---

## Cross-Category Relationships

Engineering systems are interdisciplinary.

Therefore, objectives from different categories may support, influence, or depend upon one another.

Such relationships shall be explicitly documented while preserving each objective's primary classification.

---

## Future Categories

Additional objective categories may be introduced only through formal engineering review and approval.

New categories shall:

- Address a distinct engineering purpose.
- Avoid duplication with existing categories.
- Maintain compatibility with the governance framework.
- Preserve traceability across the objective library.
